Conflicts: camx-kt, chicdk-kt, camxlib-kt
Description: CamX hardware-ISP camera integration for Tachyon (QCM6490, experimental)
 Wires up the vendor CamX stack so the IMX519 runs through the hardware ISP
 (CSIPHY -> CSID -> IFE -> IPE) instead of the RAW-only upstream camss path.
 AE, AWB, AF and lens shading all work; the kernel needs no changes, as the
 Qualcomm camera KMD already ships in the Canonical-maintained tree.
 .
 Covers both camera connectors. CSI1 and CSI2 each get their own overlay and
 sensor profile, and the two may be enabled together for dual-camera use.
 Note that CSI2 shares its connector with DSI, so using it costs the panel.
 .
 Contents:
   * per-SoC layout - /usr/lib/hw, /usr/lib/camera and 153 /usr/lib/*.so*
     links into /usr/lib/qcm6490, shipped as package payload so dpkg owns them
   * sensor description binaries for the CSI1 and CSI2 4-lane profiles
   * both DT overlays, staged under /usr/share/tachyon/dtbo. The package never
     touches /boot/dtb_a - deploying an overlay stays a user decision
   * camx-enum / camx-capture as smoke-test clients
 .
 The stock com.qti.sensorsocmap.socid_map.bin from qcom-chicdk-qcm6490 is taken
 over with dpkg-divert, so a later chicdk upgrade cannot silently restore it and
 drop the IMX519 from enumeration.
 .
 EXPERIMENTAL - this delivers the HAL3 interface only. Ordinary V4L2 clients
 (Cheese, ffmpeg, OpenCV) need a HAL3-to-V4L2 bridge that is not part of this
 package. Image tuning is borrowed from another module and is not calibrated
 for this one; auto-exposure visibly hunts as a result.
